pedia/francesco-sforza"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesco-sforza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francesco Sforza</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francesco Sforza was an Italian condottiere, son of Muzio Attendolo Sforza, who married Bianca Maria, daughter of Duke Filippo Maria Visconti of Milan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/franchino-rusca"><span class="enc-name">Franchino Rusca</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Franchino Rusca was the head of the Ghibelline Rusca family and lord of Como in the early 14th century, after long struggles with the Guelph Vittani.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/francia"><span class="enc-name">Francia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Francia was the realm of the Franks in western Europe, covering much of present-day France, the Low Countries and western Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-burton-harrison"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-burton-harrison.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis Burton Harrison</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis Burton Harrison was an American Democratic politician who served as Governor-General of the Philippines from 1913 to 1921 under President Woodrow Wilson.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-dhanis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-dhanis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis Dhanis</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis Dhanis was a Belgian officer of the Congo Free State who commanded its forces in the Congo Arab war of 1892–1894, taking Nyangwe and Kasongo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-drake"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-drake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis Drake</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis Drake (c. 1540–1596) was an English sea captain and privateer who raided Spain's American empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-farewell"><span class="enc-name">Francis Farewell</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis Farewell was a former British naval officer who in 1824 led a small party of traders from the Cape to Port Natal, founding the settlement that became Durban.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-garnier"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-garnier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis Garnier</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis Garnier was a French naval officer and explorer.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-i"><span class="enc-name">Francis I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis I was king of France from 1515 to 1547, a patron of the Renaissance and a rival of the Habsburg emperor Charles V.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-duke-of-nevers"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-i-duke-of-nevers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis I, Duke of Nevers</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis I, Duke of Nevers, born François de Clèves, was a French nobleman and soldier of the house of Cleves, which had held the county of Nevers since 1491.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis I, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis I (1708–1765), born Francis Stephen, was Duke of Lorraine from 1729 until 1737, when he gave up the duchy under the settlement of the War of the Polish…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii"><span class="enc-name">Francis II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis II was the last Holy Roman Emperor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-ii-rakoczi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis II Rákóczi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis II Rákóczi was a Hungarian noble who led the Rákóczi's War of Independence against Habsburg rule from 1703 to 1711.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-iii-duke-of-brittany"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-iii-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis III, Duke of Brittany</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis III was duke of Brittany from 1524 to 1536, the eldest son of Francis I of France and Claude of France, known as the Dauphin Francis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-iv-duke-of-modena"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-iv-duke-of-modena.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Francis IV, Duke of Modena</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Francis IV (1779–1846) was Duke of Modena and Reggio from 1814, the first ruler of the House of Austria-Este, and from 1829 also Duke of Massa and Carrara.</span></a></li></ul>
